# Security Control Integration Specification

This document defines the standard interface and architecture for integrating third-party security controls (specifically open-source tools) into the ROSI platform.

## 1. Interface Definition

Each security control integration must implement the following structure:

```javascript
{
  id: "wazuh-edr",
  name: "Wazuh EDR",
  type: "EDR", // EDR, Scanner, IDS, SIEM, etc.
  provider: "Open Source",
  status: "active", // active, inactive, error
  health: 98, // 0-100
  capabilities: [
    { id: "threat_detection", name: "Threat Detection", enabled: true },
    { id: "integrity_monitoring", name: "File Integrity", enabled: true },
    { id: "vulnerability_audit", name: "Vulnerability Audit", enabled: false }
  ],
  stats: {
    alerts24h: 124,
    lastSync: "2026-03-06T20:15:00Z"
  }
}
```

## 2. Integration Registry

A centralized `IntegrationManager` will maintain the state of all connected controls.

### Registry Functions:
- `registerControl(config)`: Adds a new tool to the dashboard.
- `toggleCapability(controlId, capabilityId)`: Enable/Disable specific features of a tool.
- `getControlStatus(controlId)`: Fetch live health and alert data.

## 3. Supported Open Source Tools (Initial Phase)

| Tool | Integration Method | Primary Capability |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Wazuh** | API / Webhook | Endpoint Security & XDR |
| **OpenVAS** | OMP / API | Vulnerability Management |
| **Suricata** | Log Ingestion | Network IDS |
| **TheHive** | API | Case & Incident Management |

## 4. UI Component: Capability Control

The dashboard will feature a "Capability Matrix" where users can toggle features ON/OFF for each tool, providing granular control over the security posture.
